Usage: [ expression

Evaluate conditional expression (requires closing ]).

OPTIONS:
  -n             string length is non-zero
  -N             file exists and has been modified since it was last read
  -z             string length is zero
  -b             file is block special
  -c             file is character special
  -d             file is a directory
  -e             file exists
  -f             file is a regular file
  -g             file has set-group-ID bit
  -G             file is owned by effective group ID (unsupported on Windows)
  -h             file is a symbolic link
  -L             file is a symbolic link
  -k             file has sticky bit
  -p             file is a named pipe
  -r             file is readable
  -s             file size is non-zero
  -S             file is a socket (unsupported for filesystem paths on Windows)
  -t             file descriptor is a terminal
  -u             file has set-user-ID bit
  -w             file is writable
  -x             file is executable
  -O             file is owned by effective user ID (unsupported on Windows)
  -eq            integer equal
  -ne            integer not equal
  -lt            integer less than
  -le            integer less than or equal
  -gt            integer greater than
  -ge            integer greater than or equal
  -a             logical and
  -o             logical or
  !              logical not
  =              string equal
  ==             string equal
  !=             string not equal
  -nt            file1 is newer than file2
  -ot            file1 is older than file2
  -ef            file1 and file2 have the same device and inode
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
